                  },
                  "linkStyle": {
                    "inherit": true,
                    "linkColor": "#514293",
                    "linkHoverColor": "#514293",
                    "linkUnderline": true,
                    "linkHoverUnderline": true
                  },
                  "text": "<span style=\"display:block;border:1px solid #1A1A1A;border-radius:10px;padding:20px 24px;background:#FFF8F3\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\">💬 <strong>What’s changing</strong></span><br><br>Your CRM is making an approved-address list compulsory. Once it’s on, <strong>only requests from approved addresses can sign in or use the API, and that includes Inkwell</strong>. It’s rolling out account by account, and your CRM will email you the date.<br><br>Separately, it will require stronger sign-in (a passkey or security key) for admins. That won’t affect the connection, but it will affect whoever manages your CRM admin.</span>",
                  "fontSize": "14px",
                  "fontFamily": {
                    "label": "Helvetica",
                    "value": "helvetica,sans-serif"
                  },
                  "color": "#1A1A1A",
                  "textAlign": "left",
                  "lineHeight": "160%",
                  "containerPadding": "16px 32px"
                }
              },
              {
